{
  "name": "rust-signal",
  "description": "A low-level interface for POSIX signal handling implemented in early-stage Rust, providing direct bindings to the sigaction system call via the libc FFI. The project demonstrates the manual configuration of signal action structures, including handler registration, mask sizing, and flag specifications for asynchronous event processing. It serves as a proof-of-concept for intercepting kernel-level interrupts and executing user-defined callback routines within a Rust runtime environment.",
